const passages = /* #__PURE__ */ JSON.parse("[{\"passageNumber\":1,\"title\":\"Company Health, Ergonomics & Remote Work Protocol\",\"subtitle\":\"Workplace safety rules and workstation setup guidelines for office and home staff\",\"text\":\"Paragraph A\\nAll contracted personnel, whether working at corporate branch premises or from home, must adhere to occupational health directives. To mitigate repetitive strain injuries (RSI) and musculoskeletal ailments, the company provides all permanent staff with an ergonomic workstation allocation. Computer display monitors must be arranged at eye level, roughly an arm's distance (50 to 70 centimeters) from the user's face, to minimize neck strain and visual fatigue.\\n\\nParagraph B\\nEmployees engaged in continuous computer operation are mandated to adopt the 20-20-20 visual rest guideline: every twenty minutes of screen engagement, staff should focus their gaze on an object at least twenty feet (six meters) away for twenty seconds. Additionally, staff must stand, stretch, or walk for five minutes every sixty minutes. The occupational health committee supplies pneumatic sit-stand desk convertors upon receipt of a certified physical therapist recommendation letter.\\n\\nParagraph C\\nRemote teleworkers must certify their home office environment annually via an online safety questionnaire. Working from informal spaces such as beds, kitchen barstools, or soft sofas for prolonged intervals is strictly prohibited during official operating hours. Should an employee suffer a physical slip, fall, or work-related injury within their designated home workspace during rostered hours, they must notify Human Resources within twenty-four hours using the online Incident Log Portal.\",\"wordCount\":350,\"questionGroups\":[{\"groupInstruction\":\"Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write:\\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this\",\"questionType\":\"true_false_not_given\",\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"g1-q1\",\"questionNumber\":1,\"prompt\":\"Computer screens should be positioned approximately one arm's length from the user.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"TRUE\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph A states monitors should be positioned 'roughly an arm's distance (50 to 70 centimeters) from the user's face'.\",\"evidence\":\"Computer display monitors must be arranged at eye level, roughly an arm's distance (50 to 70 centimeters) from the user's face\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q2\",\"questionNumber\":2,\"prompt\":\"Temporary interns receive the identical ergonomic equipment allowance as permanent staff.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"NOT GIVEN\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph A states the company provides 'all permanent staff with an ergonomic workstation allocation', but does not mention the policy for temporary interns.\",\"evidence\":\"the company provides all permanent staff with an ergonomic workstation allocation.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q3\",\"questionNumber\":3,\"prompt\":\"The 20-20-20 rule encourages workers to look at a distant object for twenty seconds.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"TRUE\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph B explains that every 20 minutes workers should 'focus their gaze on an object at least twenty feet (six meters) away for twenty seconds.'\",\"evidence\":\"staff should focus their gaze on an object at least twenty feet (six meters) away for twenty seconds.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q4\",\"questionNumber\":4,\"prompt\":\"Employees can request a sit-stand desk without providing external medical documentation.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"FALSE\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph B states sit-stand desks are supplied 'upon receipt of a certified physical therapist recommendation letter.'\",\"evidence\":\"The occupational health committee supplies pneumatic sit-stand desk convertors upon receipt of a certified physical therapist recommendation letter.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q5\",\"questionNumber\":5,\"prompt\":\"Remote employees are evaluated for home office safety once every two years.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"FALSE\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph C states remote workers must certify their home office environment 'annually', meaning once every year.\",\"evidence\":\"Remote teleworkers must certify their home office environment annually via an online safety questionnaire.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q6\",\"questionNumber\":6,\"prompt\":\"Working from a soft sofa during rostered business hours is officially forbidden.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"TRUE\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph C: 'Working from informal spaces such as beds, kitchen barstools, or soft sofas for prolonged intervals is strictly prohibited'.\",\"evidence\":\"Working from informal spaces such as beds, kitchen barstools, or soft sofas for prolonged intervals is strictly prohibited during official operating hours.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q7\",\"questionNumber\":7,\"prompt\":\"Work-related injuries occurring in home offices must be reported within 24 hours.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"TRUE\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph C says employees 'must notify Human Resources within twenty-four hours using the online Incident Log Portal.'\",\"evidence\":\"they must notify Human Resources within twenty-four hours using the online Incident Log Portal.\"}]}]},{\"passageNumber\":2,\"title\":\"Employee Professional Development and Tuition Subsidy Policy\",\"subtitle\":\"Guidelines for enrolling in accredited external courses and claiming educational expenses\",\"text\":\"The company firmly believes that continuous workforce upskilling fosters long-term organizational excellence. All full-time staff who have completed at least twelve months of uninterrupted service are eligible to apply for the Annual Professional Development Subsidy of up to £2,500 per fiscal year.\\n\\nEligibility & Application Procedure\\nTo qualify for tuition reimbursement, proposed coursework must demonstrate clear relevance to the employee's current departmental duties or align with an agreed internal career progression pathway. Recreational, hobby, or non-accredited courses are excluded from reimbursement. Prior to registering for any certification or university module, employees must submit Form TD-40 via the intranet along with course syllabus documentation and a line manager endorsement letter. Applications must be lodged at least four weeks before the registration deadline.\\n\\nReimbursement & Service Commitment\\nApproved expenses cover tuition, examination fees, and mandatory textbooks. Hardware, commuting expenses, and accommodation costs during external seminar trips are strictly ineligible. Reimbursements are processed after the employee submits an official transcript demonstrating a passing grade of 'B' or higher (or a recognized certificate of completion). In the event that an employee voluntarily resigns from the organization within twelve months of completing funded coursework, the employee is required to repay fifty percent of the subsidy.\",\"wordCount\":320,\"questionGroups\":[{\"groupInstruction\":\"Complete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8–14 on your answer sheet.\",\"questionType\":\"sentence_completion\",\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"g1-q8\",\"questionNumber\":8,\"prompt\":\"Employees become eligible for study funding after completing ____ of continuous employment.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"twelve months\",\"12 months\",\"1 year\"],\"explanation\":\"The text states: 'who have completed at least twelve months of uninterrupted service'.\",\"evidence\":\"All full-time staff who have completed at least twelve months of uninterrupted service are eligible\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q9\",\"questionNumber\":9,\"prompt\":\"The maximum financial subsidy provided per financial year is ____.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"£2,500\",\"2500\",\"2,500\"],\"explanation\":\"The text explicitly states: 'up to £2,500 per fiscal year.'\",\"evidence\":\"Annual Professional Development Subsidy of up to £2,500 per fiscal year.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q10\",\"questionNumber\":10,\"prompt\":\"Employees must complete and submit Form ____ before registering for a course.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"TD-40\",\"explanation\":\"The text states: 'employees must submit Form TD-40 via the intranet'.\",\"evidence\":\"employees must submit Form TD-40 via the intranet along with course syllabus documentation\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q11\",\"questionNumber\":11,\"prompt\":\"Funding applications must be submitted at least ____ before the course registration cut-off.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"four weeks\",\"4 weeks\"],\"explanation\":\"The text notes: 'Applications must be lodged at least four weeks before the registration deadline.'\",\"evidence\":\"Applications must be lodged at least four weeks before the registration deadline.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q12\",\"questionNumber\":12,\"prompt\":\"The subsidy will pay for tuition, exam fees, and required ____.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"textbooks\",\"mandatory textbooks\"],\"explanation\":\"The text states: 'cover tuition, examination fees, and mandatory textbooks.'\",\"evidence\":\"Approved expenses cover tuition, examination fees, and mandatory textbooks.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q13\",\"questionNumber\":13,\"prompt\":\"To receive reimbursement, candidates must achieve a minimum grade of ____.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"B\",\"'B'\"],\"explanation\":\"The text mentions 'demonstrating a passing grade of 'B' or higher'.\",\"evidence\":\"demonstrating a passing grade of 'B' or higher\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q14\",\"questionNumber\":14,\"prompt\":\"Staff who leave within one year must return ____ of the money granted.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"fifty percent\",\"50%\",\"50 percent\"],\"explanation\":\"The text states: 'repay fifty percent of the subsidy.'\",\"evidence\":\"the employee is required to repay fifty percent of the subsidy.\"}]}]},{\"passageNumber\":3,\"title\":\"Public Libraries: Transforming from Silent Archives to Civic Hubs\",\"subtitle\":\"How metropolitan public libraries evolved to serve modern digital communities\",\"text\":\"For over a century, the public library stood as a cathedral of quiet contemplation—a repository of print volumes governed by the strict shushing of stern librarians. Today, however, municipal libraries are undergoing an astonishing renaissance, reinventing themselves into vibrant civic commons that bridge the digital divide and nurture grassroots innovation.\\n\\nAs digital e-readers and internet search engines proliferated throughout the early 2000s, cynics predicted the imminent demise of physical libraries. Yet foot traffic has actually rebounded across many urban centers. Modern library patrons are not solely looking for paperback fiction; they are utilizing high-speed gigabit Wi-Fi, borrowing 3D printers in creative makerspaces, and recording podcasts in acoustic media studios. In marginalized neighborhoods, libraries act as critical social safety nets, providing free digital literacy classes for elderly citizens, resume workshops for unemployed job seekers, and quiet after-school homework sanctuaries.\\n\\nArchitecturally, modern libraries have shed their cavernous, dim corridors in favor of bright, open-plan spaces flooded with natural sunlight. Modular furniture can be rearranged to accommodate author talks, civic town halls, or bilingual children's story hours. Rather than replacing books, digital technology has expanded libraries' reach: patrons can borrow audiobooks from home via smartphone apps while visiting physical branches for human connection and community collaboration.\",\"wordCount\":380,\"questionGroups\":[{\"groupInstruction\":\"Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 15–18 on your answer sheet.\",\"questionType\":\"multiple_choice_single\",\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"g1-q15\",\"questionNumber\":15,\"prompt\":\"What did technological cynics predict in the early 2000s regarding physical libraries?\",\"options\":[\"A. They would become exclusive research spaces for academics.\",\"B. They would permanently close due to digital alternatives.\",\"C. They would increase charges for borrowing physical books.\",\"D. They would replace librarians with automated robotic sorters.\"],\"correctAnswer\":\"B\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph 2 states: 'As digital e-readers and internet search engines proliferated... cynics predicted the imminent demise of physical libraries.'\",\"evidence\":\"cynics predicted the imminent demise of physical libraries. Yet foot traffic has actually rebounded across many urban centers.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q16\",\"questionNumber\":16,\"prompt\":\"Which modern service offered by urban libraries is mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A. Free medical consultations and dental checkups\",\"B. Specialized audio recording studios for podcasts\",\"C. Commercial package delivery and courier services\",\"D. Paid overnight computer programming bootcamps\"],\"correctAnswer\":\"B\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph 2 lists 'borrowing 3D printers in creative makerspaces, and recording podcasts in acoustic media studios.'\",\"evidence\":\"and recording podcasts in acoustic media studios.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q17\",\"questionNumber\":17,\"prompt\":\"How have modern library interiors changed structurally?\",\"options\":[\"A. They have eliminated all windows to preserve paper books.\",\"B. They are designed with open layouts and abundant daylight.\",\"C. They are built entirely underground to save heating energy.\",\"D. They consist solely of soundproof individual study cubicles.\"],\"correctAnswer\":\"B\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph 3 states: 'shed their cavernous, dim corridors in favor of bright, open-plan spaces flooded with natural sunlight.'\",\"evidence\":\"shed their cavernous, dim corridors in favor of bright, open-plan spaces flooded with natural sunlight.\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q18\",\"questionNumber\":18,\"prompt\":\"How has smartphone technology complemented physical library visits?\",\"options\":[\"A. It allows users to rent audiobooks remotely while attending in-person events.\",\"B. It has forced libraries to sell off their paper inventory.\",\"C. It alerts patrons whenever they speak too loudly inside.\",\"D. It charges fines automatically to patrons' credit cards.\"],\"correctAnswer\":\"A\",\"explanation\":\"Paragraph 3 notes: 'patrons can borrow audiobooks from home via smartphone apps while visiting physical branches for human connection'.\",\"evidence\":\"patrons can borrow audiobooks from home via smartphone apps while visiting physical branches for human connection and community collaboration.\"}]},{\"groupInstruction\":\"Answer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19–20 on your answer sheet.\",\"questionType\":\"short_answer\",\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"g1-q19\",\"questionNumber\":19,\"prompt\":\"What digital creative tools can patrons borrow inside modern makerspaces?\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"3D printers\",\"3-D printers\"],\"explanation\":\"Paragraph 2 specifies: 'borrowing 3D printers in creative makerspaces'.\",\"evidence\":\"borrowing 3D printers in creative makerspaces\"},{\"id\":\"g1-q20\",\"questionNumber\":20,\"prompt\":\"What kind of furniture enables library staff to reconfigure spaces for public events?\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"modular furniture\",\"modular\"],\"explanation\":\"Paragraph 3 mentions: 'Modular furniture can be rearranged to accommodate author talks'.\",\"evidence\":\"Modular furniture can be rearranged to accommodate author talks, civic town halls, or bilingual children's story hours.\"}]}]}]");
